{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":375774,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"90e12d7c-9db7-4e4a-8f36-1b8d08faa349","total_cost_usd":1.2810555,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45769,"cache_read_input_tokens":20101,"output_tokens":31271,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45769,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":31271,"cache_read_input_tokens":20101,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45769,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45769},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":31425,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.03153,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":31271,"cacheReadInputTokens":20101,"cacheCreationInputTokens":45769,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.2495254999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"economy-balancer\",\n  \"flight\": {\n    \"dry_mass_kg\": 900,\n    \"fuel_capacity_kg\": 1200,\n    \"thrust_n\": 22000,\n    \"fuel_burn_kgs\": 10.0,\n    \"rcs_thrust_n\": 900,\n    \"rcs_fuel_burn_kgs\": 0.45,\n    \"rotation_rate_degs\": 75\n  },\n  \"cargo\": {\n    \"base_slots\": 6,\n    \"compactor_tier\": 1\n  },\n  \"reentry\": {\n    \"heat_capacity\": 100,\n    \"heat_dissipation_s\": 5,\n    \"cargo_damage_interval_s\": 3,\n    \"unstaged_heat_multiplier\": 3.5,\n    \"off_retrograde_penalty\": 1.0\n  },\n  \"ablation\": {\n    \"cycle_toll_base_pct\": 1.42,\n    \"cycle_toll_growth\": 1.25,\n    \"heat_cost_coefficient\": 0.00002,\n    \"heat_cost_exponent\": 3.0,\n    \"skim_peak\": 40,\n    \"skim_heat_multiplier\": [1.0, 0.92, 0.87, 0.86],\n    \"heat_index\": { \"suborbital\": 83, \"low\": 100, \"high\": 119 },\n    \"cost_curve\": {\n      \"suborbital\": [12.86, 13.38, 15.5, 19.3],\n      \"low\": [21.42, 20.05, 21.14, 24.75],\n      \"high\": [35.12, 30.72, 30.17, 33.46]\n    },\n    \"plate_capacity_pct\": 100,\n    \"optimal_skims\": { \"suborbital\": 0, \"low\": 1, \"high\": 2 }\n  },\n  \"landing\": {\n    \"soft_landing_ms\": 5.0,\n    \"damage_per_ms_over\": 6.0,\n    \"no_gear_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"fragile_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"parachute_drag_coefficient\": 1.8,\n    \"descent_speed_full_hold_ms\": 4.7\n  },\n  \"tow_fee\": {\n    \"free_radius_m\": 1200,\n    \"max_fee_fraction\": 0.5,\n    \"curve\": \"linear\"\n  },\n  \"eva\": {\n    \"suit_mass_kg\": 110,\n    \"jetpack_thrust_n\": 400,\n    \"jetpack_fuel_kg\": 24,\n    \"jetpack_burn_kgs\": 0.3,\n    \"base_tether_slots\": 2,\n    \"magnet_hold_force_n\": 900,\n    \"magnet_range_screens\": 0.125,\n    \"latch_jerk_coefficient\": 0.6,\n    \"swing_jerk_coefficient\": 2.5\n  },\n  \"economy\": {\n    \"launch_cost\": 100,\n    \"replate_cost_per_pct\": 2,\n    \"repair_cost_per_pct\": 5,\n    \"band_value_multiplier\": { \"suborbital\": 1.0, \"low\": 2.4, \"high\": 5.5 },\n    \"size_class_base_value\": { \"small\": 40, \"medium\": 95, \"oversized\": 340 },\n    \"fragile_value_premium\": 3.0\n  },\n  \"upgrades\": [\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 400, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 1600 },\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1100, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 2100 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 450, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 28000 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1250, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 35000 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 380, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 9 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1000, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 12 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 520, \"effect\": \"heat_capacity\", \"value\": 130 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1400, \"effect\": \"heat_capacity\", \"value\": 165 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 350, \"effect\": \"parachute_drag_coefficient\", \"value\": 2.6 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 950, \"effect\": \"parachute_drag_coefficient\", \"value\": 3.6 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 300, \"effect\": \"magnet_hold_force_n\", \"value\": 1400 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 900, \"effect\": \"magnet_hold_force_n\", \"value\": 2000 }\n  ],\n  \"balance_notes\": [\n    \"Full-hold mass doubling (GDD 2.3.5). The catalog's spawn-weighted mass per crushed-equivalent slot over the hand-tetherable shipping slice is 49210 kg-weight / 328 slot-weight = 150.03 kg per slot (suborbital 17120/160 = 107.00, low 32090/168 = 191.01). At base_slots 6 that is 900.2 kg of cargo against dry_mass_kg 900, i.e. 2.00x. base_slots stayed at 6 because the GDD's own walkthrough puts 'Cargo 4 of 6' on screen, and dry_mass_kg stayed at 900 because the Researcher's ballistic-coefficient block is built on it; the doubling is true without moving either.\",\n    \"Ablation optimum (charter step 3, GDD 2.3.1). Model evaluated, not asserted. heat_index is derived from the Researcher's interface entry speeds and the v^3 heating law: (764/813)^3 = 0.830 and (861/813)^3 = 1.188, so 83 / 100 / 119 with the low-band direct entry normalised to 100. With cycle_toll_base_pct 1.42, cycle_toll_growth 1.25, heat_cost_coefficient 2e-5, heat_cost_exponent 3.0, skim_peak 40 and skim_heat_multiplier [1.0, 0.92, 0.87, 0.86], the toll series is 1.42 / 3.20 / 5.41 / 8.19 for k = 0..3 and each skim adds a flat 2e-5 * 40^3 = 1.28. That yields cost_curve suborbital [12.86, 13.38, 15.50, 19.30] (min at index 0), low [21.42, 20.05, 21.14, 24.75] (min at index 1), high [35.12, 30.72, 30.17, 33.46] (min at index 2). The optimum therefore rises 0 -> 1 -> 2 with altitude, high is 2 as required, and no band exceeds it. Margins at the optimum are 0.52 / 1.10 / 0.55 plate-percent against the nearest alternative, so the ranking is not a rounding artefact.\",\n    \"Why growth, not a flat toll. cycle_toll_growth 1.25 is what makes the third skim lose from every band: the fourth cycle's toll alone is 1.42 * 1.25^3 = 2.77 against a marginal heat saving of only 0.76 plate-percent from the high band at that point, because skim_heat_multiplier has already saturated between index 2 and 3. A flat toll is linear in k and could not price that difference. skim_heat_multiplier itself is a considered guess, not a measurement — I run before the flight simulator. It sits slightly steeper than the charter's high-orbit sketch of [1.0, 0.95, 0.92, 0.88] because a single shared array has to average the charter's own observation that the cooling effect is larger from lower bands. If the Playtester measures it, adopt the measured array and re-price: the shape of the answer will hold, the toll constants will move.\",\n    \"Parachute descent speed at full hold (GDD 2.3.2). Terminal speed is sqrt(2*m*g0 / (rho0 * Cd * A_canopy)) with the Researcher's g0 = 4.0 and rho0 = 0.6. A base full hold is 900 dry + 900 cargo = 1800 kg, and descent_speed_full_hold_ms 4.7 requires Cd*A = 2*1800*4.0 / (0.6 * 4.7^2) = 1086 m2, i.e. parachute_drag_coefficient 1.8 over a 604 m2 canopy (a ~27.7 m disc). Empty at 900 kg the same chute gives 4.7 * sqrt(0.5) = 3.32 m/s. Note there is no canopy-area field in this schema, so the area above is the implied constant the Coder must place beside the coefficient; if the simulator instead multiplies the coefficient by the Researcher's reference_area_m2 of 3.5, the coefficient must become 310 and the arithmetic is unchanged.\",\n    \"Storage and Parachute as a pair (GDD 2.3.6). Because v scales as sqrt(m), storage tier 1 (9 slots = 1350 kg cargo, 2250 kg total) lands at 4.7 * sqrt(2250/1800) = 5.25 m/s under the base chute — over the 5 m/s line, a hard landing. Parachute tier 1 (2.6) pulls that to 4.37 m/s; storage tier 2 (12 slots, 2700 kg) lands at 5.76 m/s base, 4.79 with chute tier 1 and 4.07 with tier 2. Every Storage purchase pushes the ride home past the soft line and the matching Parachute purchase pulls it back, which is the pairing the GDD asserts, now with numbers on it.\",\n    \"Lazy run breaks even (GDD 2.3.6). A cheap suborbital piece is a small at size_class_base_value 40 * band multiplier 1.0 = 40, so launch_cost 100 is 2.5 cheap pieces, exactly the 2-3 the GDD asks for. A lazy run is a suborbital hop with a direct entry: 12.86% plate at replate_cost_per_pct 2 = 25.72, plus 100 launch = 125.72 total. Four cheap smalls pay 160, so a run that fills two thirds of the hold with the worst junk in the sky clears 34 and still owns the ship. A full six-slot hold of the same junk pays 240 for a profit of 114; two suborbital mediums plus two smalls pays 270.\",\n    \"No shear under steady tow (GDD 2.3.4, charter step 6). Steady-state tension in cable i is m_i * a where a = jetpack_thrust_n / (suit_mass_kg + sum of tethered mass), so tension_i = 400 * m_i / (110 + sum m). Since m_i is a term of the denominator's sum, tension_i is strictly less than jetpack_thrust_n = 400 N for every possible load — this is an identity, not a tuning. The worst case is one heavy piece alone: docking_collar at 700 kg gives 400 * 700/810 = 345.7 N, and the whole catalog's heaviest hand-tetherable piece, momentum_wheel_cluster at 800 kg, gives 351.6 N. magnet_hold_force_n 900 sits 2.3x above that ceiling, so steady towing can never shear at any legal load at any tether count. Shear is left entirely to the impulsive terms: latch_jerk_coefficient 0.6 shears a 300 kg piece latched above 5 m/s closing speed and a 700 kg piece above 2.1 m/s, and swing_jerk_coefficient 2.5 fires only on a deliberate reversal, both as 2.3.4 requires.\",\n    \"Flight budget (charter step 1). With ve = thrust_n / fuel_burn_kgs = 22000/10 = 2200 m/s (Isp 224 s) and the Researcher's 2400 kg unstaged fuelled mass, fuel_capacity_kg 1200 implies a ~300 kg stage dry mass and gives 2200 * ln(2400/1200) = 1525 m/s. Ascent to the suborbital band is 1057 m/s ideal (Hohmann from R = 200 km to r = 300 km, 979.8 + 77.1) or about 1300 with gravity and drag losses, and the deorbit burn to a 40 km periapsis is 41.8 m/s — so the base ship reaches band one with roughly 180 m/s of margin and nothing to spare for the band above, which is what makes fuel_tank tier 1 the first real purchase. Launch TWR is 22000/(2400*4.0) = 2.29. With a full hold at deorbit (900 dry + 900 cargo + 300 stage + residual) acceleration is still about 9.6 m/s2, so the ship stays steerable loaded, not just empty. This schema has no field for the stage's own dry mass; the 300 kg figure is implied by the Researcher's 2400 kg and must be placed beside these values by the Coder.\",\n    \"Heat capacity as the band gate (GDD 2.3.7). entry_peak reads 83 for a suborbital direct entry, 100 for a low-band direct entry and 119 from the high band, against heat_capacity 100 where cargo damage begins. So the first band is comfortable direct, the second sits exactly on the cargo-damage line and wants its one skim (92 with it), and the high band cannot be survived intact at base plate at all — heat_shield tier 1 (130) is the ticket to it. That is the GDD's 'reaching a band takes tank and thruster upgrades; surviving the return from it takes heat shield upgrades' expressed as arithmetic rather than as intent. heat_index is quoted for a nominal loaded ship; a greedy hold raises the ballistic coefficient and pushes these peaks up, which is the mass coupling 2.3.1 asks for and which the simulator should measure rather than take from here.\",\n    \"Tow fee (GDD 2.3.3). free_radius_m 1200 is the pad zone; beyond it the fee is 0.5 * (d - 1200) / (628319 - 1200), where 628319 m is half the circumference of the Researcher's 200 km planet. It is zero at the pad edge, exactly 0.5 at the antipode, clamped both ways, and applied as a deduction from haul value only — so payout runs 100% to 50% of the haul and never reaches savings, per 2.4.\",\n    \"Unstaged and off-retrograde. unstaged_heat_multiplier 3.5 stands in for the Researcher's configuration gap: ballistic coefficient 1959 kg/m2 unstaged against 171 staged means the unstaged stack drives far deeper before it decelerates, and it does so with no shield in the airflow. 3.5 keeps a shallow unstaged braking pass survivable (a suborbital skim at 40 * 3.5 = 140 still damages cargo, which is why 2.3.1's coarse passes are shallow) while making an unstaged committed entry fatal. off_retrograde_penalty 1.0 is the coefficient of the cosine law in 2.3.1: heat rate multiplier = 1 + penalty * (1 - cos theta), so 60 degrees off retrograde is 1.5x. Neither parameter reintroduces post-stage thrust; staging remains one-way and there is no field anywhere in this file that could undo it.\",\n    \"Pillar note, not a tuning. The Researcher records that orbital periods run 43 to 91 minutes and that a multi-skim descent spans hours of simulated time. No value in this file can fix that — time compression is a feature decision, and the ablation optimum of 1-2 skims from the high band is only playable if it ships. I have priced the descent as though it does.\"\n  ],\n  \"catalog_concerns\": [\n    \"insulation_blanket_wad (mass_kg 55, size_class small, band suborbital) versus crumpled_hull_panel (110) and antenna_boom_stub (75). My schema prices junk by size class and band only — there is no per-piece value field — so all three are worth exactly 40 while costing one crushed slot each. The lightest is then strictly dominant: same payout, same slot, half the landing mass. The catalog's own design note wants insulation_blanket_wad to be 'the right answer when the jetpack is dry', but under flat class pricing it is the right answer always, and the band's mass spread stops being a decision. The fix is either a per-piece value field on my side or a narrower mass spread within a class on the Debris Designer's; I cannot make it with the fields I have. The same pattern repeats in the low band between avionics_crate (200) and reaction_wheel_housing (230).\",\n    \"docking_collar (mass_kg 700, size_class medium, band low). Two on tether is 1400 kg against a 110 kg suit, so astronaut acceleration is 400/1510 = 0.26 m/s2 — 13.7x sluggier than an empty suit, and a 50 m return trip with a stop takes roughly 55 seconds of the 80 seconds of full-thrust jetpack the tank holds. I have kept jetpack_thrust_n at 400 N because raising it to make the two-collar tow pleasant would make an empty astronaut twitchy and would raise the steady-tow tension ceiling with it. The load is legal and controllable, but it is at the edge of controllable rather than inside it, and it is the one case where the catalog's mass rescaling reaches past what a hand tether comfortably supports.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":303094,"ttft_stream_ms":2159,"time_to_request_ms":202,"type":"result","duration_ms":373543,"uuid":"ed044064-aa21-4966-abb8-2329eb5786b6"}
